 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "want to / need to / have to",
   "en": "want to / need to / have to"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "want to + 동사는 '~하고 싶다', need to / have to + 동사는 '~해야 한다'입니다. he / she에는 wants to, needs to, has to를 씁니다. 하지 말아야 할 때는 mustn't + 동사를 씁니다. 하지 않아도 될 때는 don't have to를 써요.",
   "en": "Want to + verb means you would like to do it; need to / have to + verb means it is necessary. With he / she use wants to, needs to, has to. Use mustn't + verb for something not allowed. Use don't have to when it isn't necessary."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "want to + 동사",
     "I want to swim."
    ],
    [
     "need to / have to + 동사",
     "I have to study."
    ],
    [
     "he / she",
     "She wants to swim. He has to work."
    ],
    [
     "mustn't",
     "You mustn't run here."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "don't want to는 '하고 싶지 않다', don't have to는 '하지 않아도 된다'입니다.",
    "en": "Don't want to = I don't wish to; don't have to = it isn't necessary."
   },
   {
    "ko": "have to는 he / she에 has to로 바뀝니다.",
    "en": "Have to becomes has to with he / she."
   },
   {
    "ko": "want, need 뒤에는 to + 동사 원형.",
    "en": "After want and need use to + base verb."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
